WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.830
Your photo, your bio, and profiles that tell one story.

2
00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:08.870
This is the video for module two of Personal Branding and Online Presence.

3
00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:20.080
Your photo and bio are the two things almost everyone sees. On WhatsApp, your photo sits beside every message you send, so it must show your face clearly.

4
00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:31.550
Light first. Face a window, or go outside in the shade in the morning or late afternoon. Never stand with the window behind you, because your face turns dark.

5
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:38.180
Choose a plain wall or a neat workspace. Remove clutter, laundry and bright patterns.

6
00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:46.980
Hold the camera at eye level, about an arm's length away, or ask someone to help. Show your head and the top of your shoulders.

7
00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:55.530
Wear what a client would expect to see you in at work. Smile naturally, look at the lens, and take 20 or more shots.

8
00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:04.310
Crop to a square and brighten a little if needed. Avoid heavy filters, because clients should recognise you when they meet you.

9
00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:09.310
Then use that same photo on WhatsApp, Instagram, Facebook and LinkedIn.

10
00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:19.350
A bio is your positioning statement, shaped for one platform. Start from the short, medium and long versions you wrote in module one.

11
00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:23.630
Every good bio says what you do, and who it is for.

12
00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:26.390
It gives one proof point.

13
00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:31.760
And it tells the reader what to do next: how to contact you or order.

14
00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:46.020
For example, Chiamaka makes adire and ankara bags in Abeokuta. Her old bio said: Daughter of Zion. Bags. DM for price. It says nothing about style, delivery or quality.

15
00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:58.470
Her new bio: Handmade adire and ankara bags for work and owambe. Made in Abeokuta. Delivery across Nigeria in 3 to 5 days. Order on WhatsApp below.

16
00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:10.600
It is about 130 characters, inside Instagram's limit of 150. Her faith can still show in her posts, but it no longer replaces what buyers need to know.

17
00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:21.040
LinkedIn is where recruiters, employers and many business buyers check people. Fill it from the top down, starting with your photo and a simple banner.

18
00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:35.280
Your headline is not just your job title. For example, Kemi changed Customer Service Officer at a bank into Customer Experience Specialist, resolving complaints and improving service in banking.

19
00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:42.740
In About, put your strongest sentence first, because only the first two or three lines show before see more.

20
00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:52.460
In Experience, start lines with action verbs and show results, not duties. Kemi wrote: trained 8 new staff on complaint handling.

21
00:02:53.710 --> 00:03:03.330
Then use Skills, Featured and Recommendations to turn claims into proof. Make titles and dates match your CV exactly, because employers check.

22
00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:19.050
For many women in Nigeria, WhatsApp is the shop counter, and Instagram and Facebook are the shop window. WhatsApp Business is free. Add a catalogue, so customers can browse your prices without asking how much each time.

23
00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:29.770
Set a greeting message that thanks the person, points to the catalogue and says how fast you reply. Set an away message that says when you will be back.

24
00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:39.550
Save quick replies for prices, account details and delivery terms. And use labels, so no paid order is forgotten in a busy week.

25
00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:51.130
For example, Aisha sells modest fashion in Kaduna. She listed every field on every platform and found three different names, and an old phone line on Facebook.

26
00:03:52.380 --> 00:04:05.090
She chose Aisha Modest Wear everywhere, with the same photo, the same positioning line and her current WhatsApp link. Now a customer moving between her apps never wonders if it is the same person.

27
00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:22.090
Keep your account details in a quick reply, so you never mistype them. Confirm every payment in your own bank or wallet app before you send goods, because screenshots of transfers can be faked. And test your WhatsApp click-to-chat link before you publish it.

28
00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:32.250
Now your practice. Take at least 20 photos and pick the best one. Write your WhatsApp About line and Instagram bio using the four jobs.

29
00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:40.520
Rebuild your LinkedIn headline and About. Fix every mismatch across your platforms, and add at least 5 items to your catalogue.

30
00:04:40.870 --> 00:04:45.800
Screenshot each change for your after album. Now continue with the lessons below.
